  "summary_en": "India's national AI governance guidelines set seven 'sutras', recommendations across six pillars, an action plan and practical guidance. They favour a pro-innovation approach relying on existing laws, voluntary measures and techno-legal tools, and propose an AI Governance Group, expert committee, AI Safety Institute and incident database. No separate AI law is proposed.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Seven sutras: Trust, People First, Innovation over Restraint, Fairness & Equity, Accountability, Understandable by Design, Safety/Resilience/Sustainability.",
   "No separate AI law needed now; apply existing laws and make targeted amendments (IT Act, copyright, DPDP).",
   "Create AI Governance Group, Technology & Policy Expert Committee, and resource the AI Safety Institute.",
   "Develop India-specific risk classification framework and national AI incident database.",
   "Graded liability across AI value chain; voluntary frameworks, grievance redressal and transparency reports."
